# Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-GPTQ-Int4  —  TP=8 LAZY throughput, FUSED MONOLITHIC int4-MoE op
# ============================================================================
# THE A/B "fused" arm: identical to qwen35-397b-tp8-lazy-throughput.env (the STOCK
# arm) EXCEPT it turns ON the fused monolithic MoE op (HPU_MOE_FUSED_MONOLITHIC=1) and
# pins --max-num-seqs 16 (the concurrency point this experiment measures). The stock
# env is the BASELINE; run BOTH and compare aggregate tok/s at matched concurrency.
#
# WHY THIS IS THE FUSION REGIME (the diagnosis): single-stream (T=1) is host/collective-
# OVERHEAD-bound (~90% of the token is TP=8 all-reduces + host-sync), so fusion can't
# help -> the routed gather (HPU_MOE_ROUTED_K) is the single-stream lever and is left
# UNSET here. At THROUGHPUT (max-num-seqs>1, T>1) the MoE is BANDWIDTH-bound: the STOCK
# VllmMixtureOfExpertsOpWNA16 dequantizes ALL 64 local experts to bf16 -> HBM -> a
# separate mixture_of_experts gemm (the ~99us/token bf16->HBM round-trip floor). The
# fused monolithic op (torch.ops.hpu_moe_ext.fused_moe_monolithic) keeps each expert's
# int4 dequant SRAM-resident (chunked over E so each chunk's dequant is NON-PERSISTENT,
# bundled into its batch_gemm MME) and feeds it straight into the gemm — no bf16->HBM
# round-trip. That is where MoE fusion's bandwidth win actually manifests.
#
# TP=8 EP -> 512/8 = 64 experts/card. The fused op processes all 64 in ONE recipe,
# chunked by HPU_MOE_FUSED_MONOLITHIC_CHUNK (default 8 -> 8 batched sub-chains; the
# SRAM-pressure knob). It is GPTQ-symmetric int4 + silu only (which Qwen3.5-397B is);
# AWQ/non-silu would fall back to the stock op automatically.
#
# REQUIRES the built .so:  bash tpc_kernel/opbackend/build_monolithic_lazy.sh (lazy
# serve) — the lib build/libmoe_fused_monolithic_lazy.so must be present, or the wrapper
# LOUDLY warns and falls back to the stock op.
#
# DO NOT set HPU_MOE_FUSED_MONOLITHIC_VERIFY=1 in this LAZY serve: the A/B relNorm needs
# .item() which breaks lazy HPU-graph capture (it would split/blow the recipe). The
# verify is an EAGER-only debug; correctness is proven offline by tests/
# test_fused_moe_monolithic.py (relNorm<1e-2 vs the STOCK mixture_of_experts).
#
# LAUNCH:  ./serve.sh qwen35-397b-fused-monolithic
# Then benchmark concurrency (see the concurrency-benchmark command in the report /
# bench/sweep_and_watch.sh). Compare aggregate tok/s vs qwen35-397b-tp8-lazy-throughput.
IMAGE=vllm-gaudi:next
MODEL_PATH=Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-GPTQ-Int4
SERVED_NAME=qwen35-397b
MODEL_ENV="-e PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=1 -e PT_HPU_WEIGHT_SHARING=0 -e PT_HPU_ENABLE_LAZY_COLLECTIVES=true -e HPU_MARKSTEP_LAZY_ONLY=1 -e HPU_MOE_FUSED_MONOLITHIC=1 -e HPU_MOE_FUSED_MONOLITHIC_CHUNK=8 -e VLLM_ENGINE_ITERATION_TIMEOUT_S=900 -e VLLM_RPC_TIMEOUT=100000000 -e VLLM_GRAPH_RESERVED_MEM=0.2"
VLLM_ARGS="--quantization gptq_hpu --tensor-parallel-size 8 --enable-expert-parallel --max-model-len 8192 --max-num-seqs 16 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.9 --block-size 128 --async-scheduling --no-enable-prefix-caching --trust-remote-code"
